{
 "description": "Mutants for the menu of actions in the live launcher (GNOME's own menu: moving in it, Escape and the clicks are GNOME's, not listed). Not listed because GNOME does it too: giving the keyboard back to the field when the menu closes (the shell's modal stack restores it first). Not listed because equivalent or out of reach: the staleness check of an answer (the gap between asking and the answer is too short to close the window inside it, in a test), and forgetting the menu when closing (opening forgets it too). Not listed because it cannot be provoked in a live shell: a copy that fails (the clipboard always works there); it is covered by the unit tests of the controller. Also not listed because equivalent: the guard on Enter during the confirmation (a field that is not editable does not send Enter at all). Each mutant runs only the part of tests/shell/files.sh that covers it (FILES_PARTS); the whole script runs in the gate. A preview already on screen is noticed twice (its Visible state read after ShowFile, and its window at the timeout): the mutant removes both.",
 "slow": true,
